WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.617 --> 00:00:06.688
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:07.155 --> 00:00:08.623
Bwbwbwbwuuaaa!

00:00:08.623 --> 00:00:09.691
Coffeecoffeecoffee!

00:00:09.691 --> 00:00:10.525
Coffee!

00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:13.628
It's not as strong as methamphetamine
but it lets you keep your teeth.

00:00:13.628 --> 00:00:15.897
Oh, this is just a walk-in freezer.

00:00:15.897 --> 00:00:17.799
I don't want any snow cones.

00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:19.901
I can't go back.

00:00:20.268 --> 00:00:21.636
Ah, maybe there's another air vent.

00:00:21.636 --> 00:00:23.705
Then I can crawl away forever.

00:00:23.705 --> 00:00:24.405
Ice.

00:00:24.405 --> 00:00:26.441
They need one of those safety signs.

00:00:27.509 --> 00:00:29.010
Ick, pig guts.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.746
You know, I'm starting to wish I
hadn't gotten wet earlier.

00:00:31.746 --> 00:00:32.914
It's cold in here.

00:00:33.715 --> 00:00:35.550
Oh, more blood.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.718
Hey, where's the party?

00:00:36.718 --> 00:00:37.552
Oh God!

00:00:37.552 --> 00:00:39.187
Okay, lead the way. Where are we going?

00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:39.754
WHAT?!

00:00:39.754 --> 00:00:41.456
YOU'RE GOING TO HIDE IN THE CORNER?

00:00:41.456 --> 00:00:42.690
ARE YOU FIVE YEARS OLD?

00:00:43.725 --> 00:00:45.360
[bullsquid moans]

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.028
Man, now I'm almost out of bullets.

00:00:47.028 --> 00:00:47.996
Are you happy?

00:00:47.996 --> 00:00:48.930
I'm not!

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.665
You know what, you can
stay in the corner.

00:00:50.665 --> 00:00:51.566
You've earned it.

00:00:51.566 --> 00:00:54.769
I'm going to come back with a dunce cap
for you and you're going to wear it.

00:00:54.769 --> 00:00:56.771
God, look at how big that thing is.

00:00:56.771 --> 00:00:57.705
And the teeth.

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:01.543
I need more bullets; I can't be wrestling
these things with my bare hands.

00:01:01.543 --> 00:01:02.777
Or a chainsaw.

00:01:02.777 --> 00:01:04.012
That would be cool.

00:01:04.012 --> 00:01:05.747
[imitates chainsaw starting]

00:01:05.747 --> 00:01:08.049
I need a chainsaw and a hockey mask.

00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:09.751
Then we'll see who messes with...

00:01:09.751 --> 00:01:12.787
Yes.  Some more thoughtful
people left me their ammo.

00:01:12.787 --> 00:01:14.322
Is that a hand grenade?

00:01:14.322 --> 00:01:15.857
Oh my God, it is!

00:01:15.857 --> 00:01:17.859
It's like Christmas around here.

00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:21.429
People are going to crap their
pants if I wave this around.

00:01:21.429 --> 00:01:23.131
They'll do anything I want.

00:01:23.131 --> 00:01:24.599
I'm saving this for later.

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.368
I'm not going to waste this
on just anybody.

00:01:27.802 --> 00:01:30.505
Yep, back to lead salad
for the rest of you.

00:01:30.972 --> 00:01:32.040
What's that noise?

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.243
[bullsquid grunting]

00:01:35.243 --> 00:01:35.677
Quiet!

00:01:36.511 --> 00:01:39.047
Does the kitchen slaughter hogs in here?

00:01:40.415 --> 00:01:40.882
Gyah!

00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:45.053
Yeah, that's right, just
puke on my suit.

00:01:45.053 --> 00:01:46.521
It doesn't matter anymore.

00:01:46.521 --> 00:01:48.790
It's already got blood all over it.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:52.894
Most of it's not even my blood; it's
from the other alien that puked on me.

00:01:54.262 --> 00:01:57.599
I'm probably carrying a few
blood-borne diseases on my suit.

00:01:57.599 --> 00:01:59.734
I'm a walking CDC nightmare.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.603
It makes me want to hug someone.

00:02:01.603 --> 00:02:03.738
You know with all these meat
slabs hanging, I--

00:02:03.738 --> 00:02:06.174
DAMMIT! Will you stop doing that?!

00:02:06.174 --> 00:02:08.376
I can't concentrate when you do that!

00:02:08.743 --> 00:02:10.011
What was I thinking about?

00:02:10.011 --> 00:02:12.447
Oh yeah, how are they getting
those meat slabs in here?

00:02:12.447 --> 00:02:13.715
I thought there'd be a loading bay.

00:02:13.715 --> 00:02:15.450
Did they just hike them through the labs?

00:02:16.751 --> 00:02:20.088
Ah, dammit.  I've gone in circles again.

00:02:20.088 --> 00:02:21.656
This always happens.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.225
Hey, there's my air vent.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.828
Does it lead back there?

00:02:28.229 --> 00:02:29.664
Yeah, there's another dead guy.

00:02:29.664 --> 00:02:31.032
That's a good sign, right?

00:02:31.933 --> 00:02:32.834
It's kind of a bummer.

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.302
Here, I thought I was being original,

00:02:34.302 --> 00:02:36.838
but it looks like everybody's
doing the air vent thing.

00:02:36.838 --> 00:02:38.706
Why can't I start my own fad?

00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:44.312
I guess I'm the only one
that hasn't died doing this.

00:02:44.312 --> 00:02:46.014
That's kind of original around here.

00:02:46.014 --> 00:02:49.284
I still can't believe those idiots
crawled into the fan blades.

00:02:49.284 --> 00:02:51.953
I once bet my old roommate to
stick his hand in a blender

00:02:51.953 --> 00:02:53.988
and even he wasn't dumb enough for that.

00:02:56.057 --> 00:02:57.325
But you are!

00:02:57.325 --> 00:02:57.825
Hah!

00:02:58.493 --> 00:03:00.795
I bet you don't even have a
frontal lobe.

00:03:00.795 --> 00:03:02.430
I'll take that.

00:03:02.864 --> 00:03:04.866
What is that thing?
A car battery?

00:03:04.866 --> 00:03:06.868
That's not really worth pawning.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.703
It looks heavy.  I'll leave it.

00:03:09.304 --> 00:03:12.140
Ah, nuts.  I forgot to make a
dunce cap for that guy.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.976
I was hoping I could find some
poster board and a marker.

00:03:14.976 --> 00:03:17.078
Oh well, I'm not going back for him.

00:03:17.078 --> 00:03:18.780
I'm not going back for anybody.

00:03:21.149 --> 00:03:22.717
Whoa, a human skull.

00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:24.619
That would go great with my collection.

00:03:24.619 --> 00:03:27.355
Mm, maybe I'll wait.  I don't
want to clean it myself.

00:03:27.355 --> 00:03:30.725
Besides, I think Eddie said he was going
to get some more in for pretty cheap.

00:03:30.725 --> 00:03:32.093
Where the hell am I?

00:03:32.093 --> 00:03:33.261
I should be careful.

00:03:33.261 --> 00:03:36.898
If I were to die right now, I
bet no one would find my body.

00:03:36.898 --> 00:03:38.366
I can't let that happen.

00:03:38.366 --> 00:03:42.570
When I die, for my funeral, I want them
to be shooting bombs off in the air,

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.007
and have two F-16 fighter jets
doing barrel rolls overhead.

00:03:46.007 --> 00:03:47.575
That would be awesome!

00:03:47.575 --> 00:03:49.477
And, really, it's what I deserve.

00:03:49.477 --> 00:03:51.279
God, who designed this room?

00:03:51.279 --> 00:03:52.380
M.C. Escher?

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.182
It's like one of those
little gerbil mazes

00:03:54.182 --> 00:03:56.284
where you make them run
through the tubes.

00:03:56.284 --> 00:03:57.652
Except they get to cheat because th--

00:03:57.652 --> 00:03:58.119
[crunch]

00:03:58.219 --> 00:03:58.553
What?

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.922
Because their tubes are transparent.

00:04:01.489 --> 00:04:02.256
And they're gerbils.

00:04:02.724 --> 00:04:04.826
I bet you eat gerbils.

00:04:04.826 --> 00:04:06.260
WELL, I'M NOT A GERBIL!

00:04:09.297 --> 00:04:12.400
God DAMN, those things are nasty!

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.235
And it's flicking me off.

00:04:14.669 --> 00:04:15.570
I think.

00:04:17.205 --> 00:04:20.141
Why is there a ladder here
if it doesn't go anywhere?

00:04:20.141 --> 00:04:21.409
I don't know.

00:04:21.409 --> 00:04:25.213
A scientist's job is to try and make
sense of the world around him.

00:04:25.213 --> 00:04:27.582
But this whole building is crazy.

00:04:27.582 --> 00:04:28.883
Locked exits,

00:04:28.883 --> 00:04:30.752
Gordian Knot air ducts,

00:04:30.752 --> 00:04:32.787
a giant box-smashing room,

00:04:32.787 --> 00:04:34.055
it doesn't add up.

00:04:34.055 --> 00:04:36.124
The only time I feel like
I know what I'm doing

00:04:36.124 --> 00:04:38.326
is when I'm shooting or breaking things.

00:04:38.326 --> 00:04:40.895
No wonder we spend so much
money making missiles.

00:04:40.895 --> 00:04:44.532
I thought today's experiment might work,
but instead, we blew up everything.

00:04:44.532 --> 00:04:45.967
[headcrab squeals]

00:04:45.967 --> 00:04:47.201
That's what we do.

00:04:47.702 --> 00:04:50.238
Man, fighting in this
vent is kind of cramped.

00:04:50.238 --> 00:04:52.140
It reminds me of
that Jackie Chan movie

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.442
where he fights some
dude under a train car.

00:04:54.442 --> 00:04:56.077
That must've been hard.

00:04:56.978 --> 00:04:58.179
Surprise!

00:04:58.179 --> 00:04:59.847
Yo!  Security!  Wake up!

00:05:01.549 --> 00:05:03.184
Yeah, little slow, buddy!

00:05:03.184 --> 00:05:06.087
That other guy below
us is way faster than you.

00:05:06.087 --> 00:05:08.656
GUARD: Hey, don't count on the
cavalry finding us down here.

00:05:08.656 --> 00:05:09.791
GUARD: Head for the surface.

00:05:09.791 --> 00:05:11.526
Yeah, what do you think
I've been doing, Gomer?

00:05:11.526 --> 00:05:12.994
Standing around, picking my nose?

00:05:12.994 --> 00:05:14.729
GUARD: Elevators are out of order.

00:05:14.729 --> 00:05:16.030
GUARD: But we can still climb.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:18.199
Yeah, tell that to your dead coworkers.

00:05:18.199 --> 00:05:20.001
I found a few of them in the vents.

00:05:20.001 --> 00:05:20.802
OH GOD!

00:05:20.802 --> 00:05:21.736
Oh, man.

00:05:21.736 --> 00:05:24.205
I thought I almost fell
for that turret gun again.

00:05:24.205 --> 00:05:27.475
Because this stairway looks
exactly like that other one.

00:05:27.475 --> 00:05:28.643
I still don't understand why--

00:05:28.643 --> 00:05:29.677
Ah!  Ah!

00:05:30.311 --> 00:05:31.946
See, I was ready for that.

00:05:31.946 --> 00:05:33.281
You can't teach this.

00:05:33.281 --> 00:05:36.284
Let's face it, not everyone
is cut out to be me.

00:05:36.284 --> 00:05:38.586
I'm a physics-crunching badass.

00:05:38.586 --> 00:05:40.188
I'm the complete package.

00:05:40.755 --> 00:05:41.489
[lock jiggles]

00:05:41.489 --> 00:05:42.390
Oh, hey, hey!

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:43.357
Can you open this door up?

00:05:43.925 --> 00:05:45.593
Why is he adjusting his tie?

00:05:46.127 --> 00:05:48.396
Oh, it must be a one-way mirror.

00:05:48.396 --> 00:05:50.932
I can't say I'm surprised by that anymore.

00:05:50.932 --> 00:05:53.034
We're a monument to misspending.

00:05:53.034 --> 00:05:55.703
I wonder if the CEO just rubs
himself with money.

00:05:56.504 --> 00:05:58.873
Whoa!  That guy's got some moves!

00:06:00.241 --> 00:06:01.809
Yeah, see, your falling sucks!

00:06:02.243 --> 00:06:03.478
Aw, man...

00:06:04.045 --> 00:06:05.746
Why'd you have to kill that guy?

00:06:06.581 --> 00:06:08.516
He's the only cool person I've seen.

00:06:09.417 --> 00:06:12.787
Anyone who'll dive through a
window at his age is cool in my book.

00:06:13.421 --> 00:06:14.822
Grandpa was a fighter.

00:06:15.423 --> 00:06:17.725
Oh!  More grenades!

00:06:17.725 --> 00:06:19.594
I think two will do me.

00:06:19.594 --> 00:06:23.231
I'd test one right now, but I don't want
to level the building until I'm out of it.

00:06:23.231 --> 00:06:25.366
Why is it so hard to get out of
the building?

00:06:25.366 --> 00:06:29.804
It's like everywhere I turn, there's
another obstacle I have to dance around.

00:06:29.804 --> 00:06:32.273
I bet there's spikes at the
bottom of this shaft.

00:06:32.273 --> 00:06:33.407
May as well be.

00:06:34.609 --> 00:06:36.177
Hup, got another dangler.

00:06:36.177 --> 00:06:39.547
I bet somebody's wishing they could
do a pull-up right about now.

00:06:39.547 --> 00:06:42.550
Man, you have to be out of shape
not to do one pull-up.

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:45.453
You'd think that elevator shaft
would get the adrenaline going.

00:06:45.453 --> 00:06:48.189
It does with me and I'm not the
one about to die.

00:06:48.189 --> 00:06:51.292
You know, that's the nice thing
about staying fit in an academic field.

00:06:51.292 --> 00:06:53.995
You can beat up most of your
coworkers if you have to.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.465
Yeah, see, I can do a pull-up.

00:06:57.732 --> 00:06:59.133
All right!

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:00.635
Fuck.

00:07:00.635 --> 00:07:03.304
Okay, well... hey hey!  Snack machine!

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:06.374
GIVE ME SOME DORITOS!

00:07:06.741 --> 00:07:08.175
What is this, Plexiglas?

00:07:09.043 --> 00:07:10.912
A-Alright alright, I got some change.

00:07:15.016 --> 00:07:16.317
B-6.

00:07:17.151 --> 00:07:18.019
[coin clinks]

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:20.421
[vroom]

00:07:20.421 --> 00:07:23.591
[bag crinkles]

00:07:23.591 --> 00:07:26.594
[crunch crunch crunch]

00:07:26.594 --> 00:07:28.300
Nacho Cheesier.

